{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.poly_eq_zero_of_eval_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.poly_eq_zero_of_eval_pow","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L131-L140","doc":"**A polynomial vanishing at every power of `q` is zero.**  `SeminormalInequivalence`\nproves this over `ℝ` from `0 < t` and `t ≠ 1`; the content is only that `m ↦ q ^ m` has\ninfinite range, so it holds over any field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.sq_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.sq_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L117-L129","doc":"**`q ^ 2 + 1 ≠ 0` over any field**, given only that `q` is not a root of unity.\n\nThis is the lemma that keeps the general-field migration from needing an order.  Over `ℝ`\nit is `positivity`; over a general field `positivity` is unavailable *and the statement can\nfail* — but only at a fourth root of unity, which the hypothesis excludes:\n`q ^ 2 = -1` gives `q ^ 4 = (-1) ^ 2 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.pow_notRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.pow_notRootOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**A positive power of a non-root-of-unity is one.**  `(q ^ k) ^ m = q ^ (k * m)`, and\n`k * m > 0` when both are.  Needed wherever the development passes to `q ^ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L107-L108","doc":"**`q ^ 2 ≠ 1`**, the hypothesis the `ℝ` development carries explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L104-L105","doc":"**`q` is not `1`** — the `m = 1` case, named because call sites want it in this form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.zpow_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.zpow_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L71-L89","doc":"**No nonzero integer power is `1`** — the exact statement `SeminormalRep.zpow_ne_one`\nproves over `ℝ` with `Real.log_zpow`, here from the hypothesis directly.\n\n`q ≠ 0` is **not** needed: if `q = 0` then `NotRootOfUnity q` holds vacuously-ish\n(`0 ^ m = 0 ≠ 1` for `m > 0`) and `0 ^ (-k) = (0 ^ k)⁻¹ = 0 ≠ 1`, so the conclusion is\nstill true.  The `ℝ` original carries `hq0` because its `Real.log` route needs it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.pow_left_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.pow_left_injective","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L52-L69","doc":"**The powers of a non-root-of-unity are pairwise distinct.**  This is what\n`SeminormalInequivalence` extracts from `Real.log_pow` — there, by taking logs and\ncancelling; here, by cancelling `q ^ a` itself, which needs no order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.NotRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter.NotRootOfUnity","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/GenericParameter.lean#L46-L50","doc":"**`q` is not a root of unity**, in the form the seminormal construction consumes: no\npositive power is `1`.  Over `ℝ` this is implied by `q ≠ 0 ∧ q ^ 2 ≠ 1`\n(`ofSqNeOne` below); over a general field it is strictly stronger and is the hypothesis\nthe classical statement actually carries. ","signatureChunk":0}]}